= Introduction

== NSTU: A Leading University in Siberia
- One of the largest and leading universities in Siberia
#pause
- Established in 1950 as Novosibirsk Institute of Electrical Engineering (NETI)
#pause
- \~100 programs in technical, economic, and humanitarian fields
#pause
- Bachelor's, Master's, PhD, and post-doctoral levels
#pause
- \~1500 faculty members and employees
#pause
- >13,000 enrolled students

= History

== History and Achievements
- Founded in 1950 as NETI
#pause
- 2014: Awarded 5 Stars by QS Stars for innovation
#pause
- Supported by the Ministry of Education and Science of Russia
#pause
- Over 50 years: highly competitive academic community
#pause
- Research leader in nanotechnologies, new materials, energy, electronics, transport, IT, quantum technologies

= Social Life

== Campus Infrastructure
- 8 educational buildings
#pause
- 8 dormitories
#pause
- Scientific Library, publishing and printing complex
#pause
- Center of Culture, Sports Palace, swimming pool, ski base
#pause
- Clinic, sanatorium, preventorium
#pause
- Two summer camps on the Ob River and Altai

== Sports and Recreation
- One of the biggest university sports centers in Novosibirsk Oblast
#pause
- Only university in Novosibirsk with certified sports facilities in the All-Russian register
#pause
- Hosts major regional and international competitions
#pause
- Supports >30 types of sport
#pause
- Facilities: indoor gyms, swimming pool, wrestling/boxing rooms, skiing center, shooting gallery, bowling, ice rink, mini-football field, skate park, athletic field
#pause
- Suburban complexes: "Sharap" and "Erlagol"

== Cultural Life
- NSTU Cultural Center: unites all creative teams
#pause
- Hosts festivals: Student Spring, Student Fall, international jazz festival, rock festival, Fall Marathon, Theatrical Marathon, Art Revolution, KVN championship, exhibitions, concerts
#pause
- >20 student creative teams, 800 participants
#pause
- Many laureates of international, All-Russian, regional, city festivals
#pause
- 12 years winning first place at regional Student Spring in Siberia
#pause
- Teams: Academic choir, Vocal Studio, Violinist Ensemble, Jazz band, Rock Club, Folk Ballet, Dance ensemble, Show ballet, Ballroom dance studio, Break dance team, Fashion theatre, Theatre studios, Song poetry club

